---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '1 June 2026';
---

<Layout
	title="Disclaimer | GlobalsBlog"
	description="Read the GlobalsBlog disclaimer covering editorial content accuracy, calculator estimate limitations, external links, affiliate disclosure, and limitations of liability."
>
	<section class="content-page">
		<div class="content-hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">Disclaimer</p>
			<h1>Important notes about GlobalsBlog content and calculators.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				All content and tools on GlobalsBlog are published in good faith for general informational
				purposes. Please read this disclaimer carefully before relying on any article, guide, or
				calculator result for important decisions. Last updated: <strong>{lastUpdated}</strong>.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="content-grid">
			<article class="content-card">

				<h2>1. Editorial content</h2>
				<p>
					Articles across the travel, auto, beauty, and news categories are intended to inform
					and assist readers. They should not be treated as professional legal, financial, medical,
					or technical advice unless explicitly stated otherwise.
				</p>
				<p>
					We strive to publish accurate, well-researched content. However, information can change —
					prices, policies, regulations, and recommendations evolve over time. Always verify
					critical information from official or professional sources before acting on it.
				</p>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">2. Calculator and tool results</h2>
				<p>
					GlobalsBlog provides free online calculators including — but not limited to — the
					Fuel Cost Calculator, Car Loan EMI Calculator, EV Savings Calculator, Toll Calculator,
					Trip Cost Calculator, Travel Budget Planner, Road Trip Planner, and Train vs Flight
					Calculator.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>All calculator results are estimates only.</strong> Specifically:
				</p>
				<ul class="content-list">
					<li>
						<strong>Car Loan EMI:</strong> EMI calculations use the standard reducing-balance
						formula but do not account for processing fees, GST, insurance add-ons, prepayment
						charges, or other terms specific to individual lenders. Always confirm the final
						EMI and total cost with your bank or NBFC before signing any loan agreement.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Fuel Cost:</strong> Results depend entirely on the mileage and fuel price
						values you enter. Real-world fuel consumption varies with driving conditions, vehicle
						condition, AC use, load, and road type.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Toll Charges:</strong> Toll estimates are based on approximate NHAI average
						rates per vehicle category. Actual toll charges vary by highway, state, toll plaza
						operator, and season. Use the official NHAI portal or FASTag app for exact rates.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>EV Savings:</strong> Savings projections assume consistent monthly usage,
						stable electricity rates, and no changes to petrol prices. Actual savings may vary
						significantly based on charging habits, battery degradation, and market conditions.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Trip, Road Trip & Budget Calculators:</strong> Cost estimates are based
						on average market rates and user-provided inputs. Actual travel costs depend on
						seasonal pricing, booking timing, destination, travel style, and individual spending.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Train vs Flight:</strong> Fare comparisons use prices you input manually.
						Actual fares fluctuate with availability, season, and booking class.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					<strong>None of the calculator results constitute financial, investment, or professional
					advice.</strong> For significant financial decisions such as car loans or large travel
					expenditure, consult a qualified financial adviser.
				</p>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">3. Accuracy and updates</h2>
				<p>
					Articles and calculator defaults (example values, rate estimates) may be updated,
					corrected, or expanded over time. Some posts may become outdated after publication.
					The "last updated" date on articles, where shown, reflects the most recent revision.
				</p>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">4. Affiliate, advertising & sponsored content</h2>
				<p>
					GlobalsBlog displays advertising through Google AdSense. The site may also publish
					sponsored or commercially-supported content in the future. Where applicable, such
					relationships will be disclosed clearly within or adjacent to the relevant content.
					Advertising revenue does not influence editorial decisions or calculator methodologies.
				</p>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">5. External websites</h2>
				<p>
					GlobalsBlog may link to external websites for reference or convenience. We are not
					responsible for the content, accuracy, availability, or privacy practices of any
					third-party website. Following an external link is at your own discretion.
				</p>

				<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">6. Limitation of liability</h2>
				<p>
					To the fullest extent permitted by law, GlobalsBlog and its operators accept no
					liability for any direct, indirect, or consequential loss or damage arising from
					your use of the site, its articles, or its calculator results — including but not
					limited to financial loss resulting from decisions made based on calculator estimates.
				</p>

			</article>

			<aside>
				<div class="content-card content-card-accent" style="position:sticky;top:1.5rem">
					<h2>Key takeaways</h2>
					<ul class="content-list">
						<li>Articles are informational — not professional advice</li>
						<li>Calculator results are <strong>estimates only</strong></li>
						<li>Car loan EMI does not include bank fees or insurance</li>
						<li>Toll estimates are based on NHAI averages, not exact rates</li>
						<li>Always verify important information with official or professional sources</li>
					</ul>

					<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">Contact for concerns</h2>
					<p>
						If you believe any content or calculator result is inaccurate or misleading,
						please contact us:
					</p>
					<p>
						<a href="mailto:contact@globalsblog.com">contact@globalsblog.com</a>
					</p>
					<p style="margin-top:0.75rem">
						<a href="/contact-us">Contact page →</a>
					</p>

					<h2 style="margin-top:1.5rem">Related pages</h2>
					<ul class="content-list">
						<li><a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a></li>
						<li><a href="/terms-and-conditions">Terms and Conditions</a></li>
						<li><a href="/tools">Calculator tools</a></li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
